## (f) cause
Verdict: the derivation misses the report on a RULE MISS, at the layout level. The report IS in the derivation's inputs (e), and the stored objects are NOT stale (e: stored equals today's code on today's inputs, and every stored object postdates the report's fetched_at of 2026-09-25 02:05:52Z). The label regex (continuation.py 132) is applied to a pdf locator that is a whole PAGE, anchored at the start of the page text. The page text begins "1 \n \nUnitedHealth Group Incorporated (UNH-US) \n2Q26 earnings update", so the one line "Recommendation: Maintain positions in PFOE and DIVZ" at offset 75 is never tested. The RULED text in the module docstring (line 47 onward) assumes a page "starting RECOMMENDATION"; this report's page does not start that way. The text it states is PFOE (and DIVZ), so with a line-level read the rule would yield fund_of_record PFOE and last_stated_position "Maintain positions in PFOE and DIVZ". By (e), a continuation rebuild of UNH on the current code and inputs yields the same absent fields, and the dossier copies them (dossier.py 1501-1502), so a rebuild alone does not repair UNH; the rule must change first. No other cause is supported: no_stated_position is refuted (the text exists), report_not_in_items is refuted (rows=1), stale_object is refuted (5 of 5 equal).

