Keys written, continuation: amgt/harvest/gold/research-continuation/security_key=<KEY>/<sha16>.json, sha16 = sha256 over the canonical {method_version, inputs}, first 16 hex (continuation.py 159-165, object name at 949). Writer: gold.gold_put with IfNoneMatch="*" (gold.py 70-). It NEVER overwrites: the same name with the same bytes is a no-op (existed); the same name with different bytes raises GoldImmutableError. A changed input set or method gives a NEW name beside the old object (versioned, not overwritten).
Keys written, dossier: amgt/harvest/gold/research_dossier/security_key=<KEY>/as_of=<as_of>.<sha16>.json (dossier.py 1682-1684). Same never-overwrite rule. dossier write_one first reads the newest stored object and writes NOTHING when its inputs equal the fresh inputs and its method equals METHOD_VERSION (1651-1680).
Lock: none. gold.gold_put is one conditional put (gold.py 70-); no lock file was found in the two writers.
Trigger or schedule: none in code. lib/research/corpus/production_sequence.py STEPS (57-68) is the ruled runner: step 5 continuation --write, step 9 dossier --write; it is run by hand per its header. comp-find census of production_sequence (corpus=all): 9 hits, none a scheduler.
REBUILD_ONE_SECURITY: yes for dossier (CLI --security-key); yes for continuation only by calling the function write_one(security_key) from Python, because the continuation CLI has no one-name write.
REBUILD_NEEDS_EXCLUSION_INPUT: yes. The misfiled-reports list is NOT in lib at HEAD (git grep MISFILED_REPORTS under lib: no hits); it lives only in the gateway (MISFILED_REPORTS, harvest_research.py 201-210). The two listed reports are silver rows of KMB_US_Equity: 1a3b56044db679a5 (class B, IDVZ) and fbd50086c4065785 (class B, IDVZ), both in part_20260923T044515Z.parquet. Both would enter KMB's items with the code as written. KMB's gold objects and extractions were NOT fetched (outside this cell's UNH scope), so their effect on stored KMB objects is not measured here.

